      "content": "\"goblin-like\" chaotic elements? \n\nI'm a bit confused by that phrasing. We are trying to present a professional, enterprise-grade technical brief to a VP. Using terms like \"goblin-like\" to describe network latency or race conditions feels very out of place and unprofessional. \n\nCan we remove all those metaphors and just stick to the technical terminology? I need this to be strictly about distributed systems theory and mitigation strategies.",
